# Party banter on the Old Svalich Road and at Tser Pool. Each node opens with an `if` gate: it is eligible only while
# its condition holds, and plays once. Party members speak through interjections; guests (Ireena, Ismark) speak as
# themselves, so their lines sit behind `guest:` conditions. An exchange between companions names them in its gate.

~ banter_left_hanging
if flag.crossroads_gallows_seen and not flag.nicu_cut_down and not flag.crossroads_dead_cleared and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We passed a hanged boy at the crossroads and left him to the crows. I prayed as we walked. It wasn't enough.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Then we go back and cut him down. Nobody gets left behind. Not even the dead ones.
elif flag.crossroads_gallows_seen and not flag.nicu_cut_down and not flag.crossroads_dead_cleared
interject class:cleric: We walked past a hanged boy and left him for the crows. I'd like that on someone's conscience other than mine.
interject tag:blunt: It's on all of ours. We go back and cut him down, or we don't. Decide.
endif
-> END

~ banter_nicu_buried
if flag.nicu_cut_down and flag.nicu_rites_said and name:wren_featherfoot and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:wren_featherfoot: First person we've buried in this valley who's actually stayed buried. Low bar. We cleared it.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: He's at rest, Wren. Words help. So does a straight grave, and someone who stays to dig it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_nicu_risen
if flag.crossroads_dead_cleared and name:thistle and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:thistle: We left him up. He came down by himself, and angry. Next one, we cut down.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Agreed. Hereinafter, all hanged persons shall be cut down. I'm writing it in. In ink.
endif
-> END

~ banter_luminita
if flag.luminita_confessed and name:kip_smudgewick and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:kip_smudgewick: She gave him the horse to sell. Now she thinks she tied the rope herself.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: She didn't. She's sad, and she thinks sad means guilty. Somebody should keep telling her it doesn't.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: ...Yes. Somebody should tell her that.
endif
-> END

~ banter_misdirect
if flag.stanimir_misdirects and name:wren_featherfoot and name:thistle
interject name:wren_featherfoot: The fiddler's telling the castle we went east. That's a man sticking his neck out for us.
interject name:thistle: Or selling us the minute it pays better. He smells like both.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Both, then. I'll allow it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_godrick
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "godrick_pendlebrook" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:ratatoille
interject name:ratatoille: Godrick. About the reading. Letters are only a recipe for sounds. I could teach you, evenings. I'd be very patient. Probably.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Would you? I'd like that. I'd like that very much.
elif flag.eva_truth_teller == "godrick_pendlebrook" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You keep your oath without a book, Godrick. The words live where they ought to: in you.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Oh. Well. When you say it like that, it doesn't sound so bad.
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_liriel
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "liriel_dawnsong" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:thistle
interject name:thistle: Sunbeam. Scared of the dark. Here, of all places.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Yes. In hindsight, it was a poor choice of country.
interject name:thistle: I'll sleep by your lamp, then. Dark has to get past me first.
elif flag.eva_truth_teller == "liriel_dawnsong" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: My lady. I'll keep the lantern lit every night. I'm the tallest, so it'll light more.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: That isn't how lanterns work, Godrick. Thank you. It helps more than you know.
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_thistle
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "thistle" and name:thistle and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Thistle. You belong with us. That's a somewhere. It's got a cook and everything.
interject name:thistle: ...Shut up, Big.
elif flag.eva_truth_teller == "thistle" and name:thistle and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: For what it's worth, you'd do well in a market town. People trust a loud voice.
interject name:thistle: ...Pastries, though?
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Every market day. I'll show you the good stalls. No obligation.
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_ratatoille
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "ratatoille" and name:ratatoille and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Ratatoille. Feeding people is holy work. When I say grace over your cooking, I mean every word.
interject name:ratatoille: ...Please don't tell the academy. Or do. No. Don't.
elif flag.eva_truth_teller == "ratatoille" and name:ratatoille and name:thistle
interject name:thistle: Cook more, then. Cast less. I'll eat it.
interject name:ratatoille: That is not the point. You have entirely missed the... What would you like tonight?
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_wren
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "wren_featherfoot" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You never had your last lesson, you said. Perhaps you're having it now, Wren. Slowly.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Rude. Lovely, but rude.
elif flag.eva_truth_teller == "wren_featherfoot" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Sir Pellam died before he'd finished with me, too. I think they leave us to finish ourselves.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: ...Yeah. All right. Thanks, big man.
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_kip
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "kip_smudgewick" and name:kip_smudgewick and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Your da said no so you'd not have to. You said yes so he'd not have to. That's a family, that.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: ...Apricot? No reason. I just need to hand you something.
elif flag.eva_truth_teller == "kip_smudgewick" and name:kip_smudgewick and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You did a wrong thing for a loving reason, Kip. I'll pray for you. No, I insist.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Is that in my favour, or against? Sorry. Professional habit.
endif
-> END

~ banter_truth_other
if flag.eva_truth_teller == "other"
interject tag:curious: Whatever you told the old woman, you don't have to tell us. But you could. If you wanted.
interject tag:loyal: Leave it. It was paid for. It's spent.
endif
-> END

~ banter_forced_reading
if flag.eva_reading_paid == "forced" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: We frightened an old woman into reading for us. Let it be written that I was against it.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: It's written. In her face. People remember who leaned on them, and they remember the price.
endif
-> END

~ banter_brawl
if flag.tser_pool_brawl_won and name:wren_featherfoot and name:ratatoille
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Only music in the whole valley, and we stopped it. Nice work, everyone.
interject name:ratatoille: They swung first. I'm almost certain. I was mid-incantation at the time.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Keep saying it, Rat. One of us will believe it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_eva_ireena
if flag.eva_recognized_ireena and guest:ireena
Ireena: "You have come round again." What did she mean by that? Don't answer. I don't think I want the answer.
if name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Then we won't answer. We'll only stay close, as long as you'll have us.
else
interject tag:loyal: Nobody's answering. We're just staying close.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_question
if flag.eva_question == "escape" and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: One road out, and it goes through him. Good. I like a plan with one road.
elif flag.eva_question == "escape"
interject tag:blunt: No door out but through him. Good. I prefer a plan with one road.
elif flag.eva_question == "weakness" and name:ratatoille
interject name:ratatoille: The three things, the friend and the room. All at once, in the right order. It's a recipe. A horrible one.
elif flag.eva_question == "weakness"
interject tag:scholarly: The three things, the friend and the room. She made it sound like a recipe. Horrible, but a recipe.
elif flag.eva_question == "ireena" and name:thistle
interject name:thistle: No high places. No still water. Easy. I'll watch her feet.
elif flag.eva_question == "ireena"
interject tag:loyal: Keep her away from heights and still water. We can do that. We can do that every single day.
elif flag.eva_question == "why" and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: He was bored, so he sent for the entertainment. I've played worse rooms. Not many.
elif flag.eva_question == "why"
interject tag:cheerful: Because he was bored. We're the entertainment. I've had worse jobs. Not many.
endif
-> END

~ banter_question_order
if flag.eva_question == "order" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I asked after the Order, and she answered in a riddle. I'm bad at riddles. Was that a yes?
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel talked in riddles too. Usually meant "yes, but you won't like it."
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: But it's a yes!
elif flag.eva_question == "order" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: She answered me sideways about the Order. Seers do that, don't they?
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: They do. It lets you hear the answer when you're ready to.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Right then! I'll be ready by the time we find them.
endif
-> END

~ banter_question_dawn
if flag.eva_question == "dawn" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:thistle
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I didn't truly need her answer. I only wanted to hear someone else say the dawn comes.
interject name:thistle: Dawn's coming! There. Loud enough?
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Quite loud enough, dear heart. Thank you.
elif flag.eva_question == "dawn" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:ratatoille
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: I knew the answer before I asked. I only wanted to hear it in someone else's mouth.
interject name:ratatoille: Technically, I am a diviner. I foresee breakfast. Breakfast implies a morning. Voilà.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: That is the kindest bad theology I have ever heard. Thank you.
endif
-> END

~ banter_question_fen
if flag.eva_question == "fen" and name:thistle and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:thistle: She answered about Grandda. Don't ask what she said.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: I won't. I'll just walk on this side of you. The windy side.
interject name:thistle: ...Thanks, Big.
elif flag.eva_question == "fen" and name:thistle and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:thistle: Don't ask me what she said about Grandda. Not yet.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Wasn't going to. Race you to that tree instead?
interject name:thistle: ...Go.
endif
-> END

~ banter_question_wizard
if flag.eva_question == "wizard" and name:ratatoille and name:thistle
interject name:ratatoille: She knows where the Wizard of Wines is. A seer of her standing! I must practise my bow.
interject name:thistle: You'll leave us for him? Who cooks?
interject name:ratatoille: An apprentice has evenings off. I assume. I'll cook in the evenings.
elif flag.eva_question == "wizard" and name:ratatoille and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:ratatoille: The Wizard of Wines is real, and in this valley. My apprenticeship is as good as signed.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Read it first, whatever it is. Read the small print, that's what Mum says.
interject name:ratatoille: Kip. Genius does not come with small print.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Everything comes with small print.
endif
-> END

~ banter_question_kasimir
if flag.eva_question == "kasimir" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Will you open Sorrel's letter before you hand it over? Just a peek. For the paperwork.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Kip. I'm a scoundrel, not a monster. It goes to his brother sealed.
elif flag.eva_question == "kasimir" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: So Kasimir is a real man, somewhere in this valley. Not only a name on a letter.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Real man, real letter. Easy. Walk up, hand it over, done.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: You've carried it this far, Wren. You'll carry it the rest.
endif
-> END

~ banter_question_contract
if flag.eva_question == "contract" and name:kip_smudgewick and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I asked if there's a way out. She answered like a solicitor. That's either very good or very bad.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: If the devil comes for you, I'll fight him. That's three times I've offered now.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Legally inadvisable. Deeply appreciated. Please keep offering.
elif flag.eva_question == "contract" and name:kip_smudgewick and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:kip_smudgewick: She answered like a solicitor. Notwithstanding, I think there was a door in it somewhere.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Then we find the door. I've squeezed through smaller ones for less.
endif
-> END

~ banter_reading
if tarokka.drawn and tarokka.ally == darklord and name:wren_featherfoot and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:wren_featherfoot: No friend in the cards. Fine. We've got us.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Then we'll be our own ally. I'll be the big one.
elif tarokka.drawn and name:ratatoille and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:ratatoille: Her spread is crude, her technique unorthodox, and she is right. I can feel it. I hate it.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Gently, Ratatoille. Envy is only admiration that hasn't eaten yet.
endif
-> END

~ banter_treasure_given
if flag.tser_treasure_given and name:kip_smudgewick and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:kip_smudgewick: She kept it in a chest behind her chair. For years. I'd have sold it inside a week.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: She was waiting for the right hands, Kip. Keep yours on it, not on a price.
endif
-> END

~ banter_robbery
if flag.vistani_robbed and flag.vistani_repaid and name:kip_smudgewick and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:kip_smudgewick: We robbed the only friendly fire in the valley, then paid it back. With interest. I added interest. I felt I should.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Good. Next time we rob the castle. Bigger pockets.
elif flag.vistani_robbed and flag.stanimir_deceived and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Stanimir thinks one of his own boys took the gold. Some poor lad will be shouted at, for us.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: The old woman knew, though. She looked right at me. Nobody looks right at me.
endif
-> END

~ banter_strahd_road
if flag.strahd_road_encounter == "violent" and name:thistle and name:ratatoille
interject name:thistle: Hit him square. Hit fog. Cheat!
interject name:ratatoille: Mist form. Textbook. Next time, sunlight. I will find out where one buys sunlight.
elif flag.strahd_road_encounter == "courteous" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: We were polite to him. Sir Pellam always said be polite to a man before you hit him.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Did he say how long before?
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: ...No. He never said.
elif flag.strahd_road_encounter == "defiant" and name:kip_smudgewick and name:ratatoille
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Off my road, he says. I looked. No toll house, no milestones with his name. No paperwork at all.
interject name:ratatoille: He doesn't need paperwork. He owns the wolves.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: ...That is a kind of paperwork.
elif flag.strahd_road_encounter == "shield"
Ireena: You stood in front of me. Don't do it again. ...Thank you.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Sorry, my lady. I'll do it again.
endif
elif flag.strahd_road_encounter == "silent" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:thistle
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Nobody said a word to him. Was that brave, or were we terrified?
interject name:thistle: Both. You go quiet near a bear. That's clever, not scared.
endif
-> END

~ banter_anca
if flag.anca_fate == "unwarned" and name:liriel_dawnsong and name:ratatoille
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Two marks on that old woman's throat, and we let her son wheel her into a churchyard. We should have said.
interject name:ratatoille: I knew what they were. I've read about them for years. And I said nothing. Next time I say it out loud.
elif flag.anca_fate == "staked" and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: The lad didn't watch. Good. I watched for him. Better I keep that than him.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: I gave him an apricot after. It was all I had.
endif
-> END

~ banter_procession
if flag.dead_procession_turned and name:thistle and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:thistle: They put the box down and walked off into the fields. Like they were going home.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: They were. Be at peace, all of you.
elif flag.dead_procession_destroyed and name:kip_smudgewick and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Six of them carrying one coffin, and they'd measured us for it. I don't like being measured.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Bet they'd have done you a good price.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Not funny. ...Slightly funny.
endif
-> END

~ banter_raven
if flag.raven_fed and name:thistle
interject name:thistle: That raven nodded at us. Proper nod. Then off toward the vineyards, looking back. It wants following.
interject species:elf: Some birds in old places carry more than seeds. I'd follow it, one day.
elif flag.raven_fed
interject tag:curious: That raven nodded at us. A bird nodded. And then it flew off toward the vineyards like it wanted us to follow.
interject species:elf: Some birds in old places carry more than seeds. I'd follow it, one day.
elif flag.raven_harmed and name:ratatoille and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:ratatoille: We hurt the one creature in this valley that wasn't trying to kill us. Every augury I know calls that a bad sign.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: It might have been his. His bird, I mean. Possibly.
interject name:ratatoille: It wasn't. A diviner knows an omen when it looks at him. That one looked kind.
elif flag.raven_harmed
interject class:druid: We hurt the one creature in this valley that wasn't trying to kill us. The trees noticed.
interject tag:blunt: It might have been his.
interject class:druid: It wasn't.
endif
-> END

~ banter_hunters
if flag.hunters_befriended and flag.werewolf_rumor and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:thistle
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Wolves on two legs, a den in the hills, and a mother they pray to. That's not a pack. That's a parish.
interject name:thistle: Grandda says a wolf that prays has forgotten which one it is.
elif flag.hunters_befriended and flag.werewolf_rumor
interject tag:veteran: Wolves that walk on two legs, a den in the hills, and a mother they pray to. That's not a pack. That's a regiment.
elif flag.hunters_fought
interject class:cleric: Frightened men with bows, and we cut them down on a road. They thought we were his. Maybe they weren't entirely wrong.
elif flag.werewolf_rumor
interject class:ranger: Claw marks higher than a man can reach. Something in these woods stands up when it wants to.
endif
-> END

~ banter_falls
if flag.ireena_falls_memory and guest:ireena
Ireena: At the falls. I wasn't going to jump. I want you to know that. I just couldn't remember, for a moment, whose feet they were.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: Yours. I know your tracks now. I'd know them anywhere.
else
interject tag:loyal: Then we'll remember for you. They're yours. Both of them.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_werewolf
if flag.falls_werewolf_slain and name:thistle and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:thistle: That wolf at the falls was waiting. For one of us to stand too near the edge.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Good thing none of us is the type to stand near edges.
interject name:thistle: You did a handstand on the edge.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ismark_road
if guest:ismark and visited:tser_pool
Ismark: Do you know, I'd never been to Tser Pool? Twenty years, half a day's walk. Father always said the Vistani would steal my boots.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: They didn't, though! Look. Boots. Both of them.
else
interject tag:cheerful: They didn't, though. You've still got your boots.
endif
Ismark: I've checked twice.
endif
-> END
